# Walkthrough — Google Meet & Google Drive Integration

We have successfully integrated Google Meet counseling sessions and Google Drive document storage. This completely replaces AWS S3 and binds both Calendar and Drive services to the counselor's connected Google account.

## Changes Made

### 1. Backend API & Database (`hytech_visa_backend/`)
- **Dependencies ([requirements.txt](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/requirements.txt))**: 
  - Added: `google-auth`, `google-auth-oauthlib`, `google-api-python-client`, and `cryptography`.
  - Removed: `boto3` (AWS S3 client).
- **Settings & Config ([config.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/core/config.py) & [.env](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/.env))**:
  - Removed all `AWS_*` settings.
  - Added `drive.file` to `GOOGLE_SCOPES`.
  - Added `COUNSELOR_USER_ID` to target the counselor's OAuth token for applicant uploads.
- **Models**:
  - `CounselorGoogleAccount` ([counselor_account.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/models/counselor_account.py)): Stores counselor calendar/drive credentials.
  - `Meeting` ([meeting.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/models/meeting.py)): Stores meeting sessions.
  - `Document` ([document.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/models/document.py)): Replaced S3 `storage_key`/`storage_url` columns with `drive_file_id`, `drive_view_link`, and `drive_folder_id`.
- **Alembic Migrations**: Upgraded schema changes successfully.
- **Unified Service ([google_service.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/services/google/google_service.py))**: Core calendar (Meet conferencing) and Drive (folder establishment, file uploads, permissions granting) operations.
- **Routers**:
  - `google` ([google.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/api/v1/routes/google.py)): Authorization flow and callback HTML page.
  - `meetings` ([meetings.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/api/v1/routes/meetings.py)): Counseling booking, rescheduling, and cancellations.
  - `documents` ([documents.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/api/v1/routes/documents.py)): File upload endpoint modified to target Google Drive.
  - Registered all routers inside [main.py](file:///d:/git/visa/hytech_visa_backend/app/main.py).

### 2. Flutter Student Client (`hytech_student_app/`)
- **Dependencies ([pubspec.yaml](file:///d:/git/visa/HyTech-Education/app/student%20app/hytech_student_app/pubspec.yaml))**: Added `url_launcher`.
- **Models**:
  - `MeetingModel` ([meeting_model.dart](file:///d:/git/visa/HyTech-Education/app/student%20app/hytech_student_app/lib/core/models/meeting_model.dart))
  - `DocumentModel` ([document_model.dart](file:///d:/git/visa/HyTech-Education/app/student%20app/hytech_student_app/lib/core/models/document_model.dart)): Added `driveViewLink` and `driveFolderId`.
- **API Clients & BLoC**:
  - `MeetingsApi` and `MeetingsBloc` manage schedules. Provided in `MultiBlocProvider` in [main.dart](file:///d:/git/visa/HyTech-Education/app/student%20app/hytech_student_app/lib/main.dart).
- **Screens**:
  - `AppointmentsScreen` ([appointments_screen.dart](file:///d:/git/visa/HyTech-Education/app/student%20app/hytech_student_app/lib/features/appointments/presentation/appointments_screen.dart)): High-fidelity tabbed interface for viewing upcoming sessions or booking a new one.
  - `StudentHome` ([student_home.dart](file:///d:/git/visa/HyTech-Education/app/student%20app/hytech_student_app/lib/features/home/presentation/student_home.dart)): Connects the home screen "Upcoming Appointment" card dynamically to the nearest meeting.
  - `DocumentsScreen` ([documents_screen.dart](file:///d:/git/visa/HyTech-Education/app/student%20app/hytech_student_app/lib/features/documents/presentation/documents_screen.dart)): Triggers case documents fetch, cross-references files, and adds a premium "View on Drive" action for uploaded items.

## Verification & Validation
- **Database Schema Validation**: Database tables are successfully updated in PostgreSQL and migrations are current.
- **Backend Import Verification**: The pytest run confirms all dependencies and endpoints compile and import cleanly.
- **Graceful Fallbacks**: Created a fallback mechanism for both calendar booking and document uploads that automatically generates mock data for local testing when OAuth connections are pending.
